LINQ TakeWhile() vs Where() — Same Condition, Different Results!

Both methods filter collections, but there's an important difference.

🔸 Where() checks the entire sequence and returns all matching elements.

🔸 TakeWhile() returns elements only until the first condition fails. Once it fails, it stops, even if later elements match.

The order of elements matters when using TakeWhile().

✅ Use Where() when you need all matching elements.

✅ Use TakeWhile() when you need consecutive matching elements from the beginning of a sequence.
